  "limitations": [
    "Legacy monotonic elapsed fields are collected unconditionally even with opt-in hierarchical timings disabled; these are nested native-call wall intervals, not CPU counters.",
    "One actual CGU/one worker makes the selected object receipt unambiguous; no summation of overlapping worker spans is used.",
    "total_ns ends while constructing the receipt, before RAII native handles are dropped. It is not full backend or full CLI time.",
    "llvm_unclassified_ns is a per-row subtraction covering setup, verifier and other unlabelled native-call work; it does not identify any individual missing stage.",
    "outside_llvm_receipt_ns includes frontend, lowering, diagnostic rendering, native-handle cleanup, linking, publication and process overhead; no cause is assigned to it.",
    "Each metric is aggregated independently. Weighted medians of components need not add to the weighted median of their sum; deltas are diagnostic and cannot exactly partition total regression.",
    "Stage wall intervals do not explain generated-program runtime quality or distinguish register allocation, code size, instruction selection and layout effects.",
    "Author interpretation of existing formal receipts only; the formal NoGo decision and product-gate status are unchanged."
  ],
  "interpretation": [
    "The fixed O0 recipe added promotion work, while the full CLI window did not demonstrate a compile-time gain. The optimize and emit fields below indicate where the native-call tradeoff occurred; they are not a separate performance result.",
    "Existing runtime NoGo is a separate generated-code-quality observation; the legacy compilation receipts alone do not establish its mechanism."
  ]
